    "stem": "Parth builds a row of pentagon frames with ice-cream sticks. Shape $1$ uses $5$ sticks, Shape $2$ uses $9$ sticks, and Shape $3$ uses $13$ sticks.\n\nWhich two claims correctly name the countable feature that produces the related number sequence $5$, $9$, $13$, $\\ldots$?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Count the ice-cream sticks that make up each whole shape; repeating that same count gives $5$, $9$, $13$, $\\ldots$.",
      "B": "Count the sticks in Shape $1$ only, then reuse that same count for every later shape.",
      "C": "The same structural feature — the sticks of each whole frame — must be counted in every shape of the sequence.",
      "D": "Pick the printed numeral $13$ alone because it is the largest number shown."
    },
